GARDEN v15.9 DOCUMENTATION REBUILD — STRUCTURAL REVIEW PACKET
Date: 2026-09-18
Purpose: improve documentation only; preserve semantics exactly.
Source authority: current clean v15.9 five-file design.
Models are editorial reviewers, not semantic authorities.

USER GOALS
1. Retain all design data.
2. Remove duplicate data and explanations with no extra value.
3. Rewrite for human readability.
4. Improve structure/navigation.
5. Keep theory versioning/status consistent.
6. Restore canonical naming definition: GAIA = Garden Artificial Intelligence Architecture.
7. Produce a full Garden design, not a release-history or review-history archive.

NON-NEGOTIABLES
- Do not weaken or reinterpret any normative rule.
- Do not invent new Garden semantics.
- One semantic fact should have one canonical owner; other files cross-reference it.
- Historical/review/process commentary should not remain in publication unless it is itself normative.
- Preserve explicit CURRENT / QUALIFIED / EXPERIMENTAL / RESEARCH / DEFERRED / RETIRED state.
- Preserve all active anchors, rights, invariants, schemas, tests, proof obligations, theory definitions, profile boundaries and deferred items.
- Specification != implementation != executed conformance != empirical validation != certification.
- No top-level Engine/Core Object/Core Relation/authority source may be created by documentation cleanup.
- Annexure is the normative owner for registries/global cross-layer rules; other files should avoid duplicate normative copies.
- GAIA naming definition must be explicit once; later uses should use GAIA.

CURRENT FILE INVENTORY
User: 114 KB; human design; major sections H-00..H-15 plus CPI/CDDT/OCF/MSC/TML/CMUR/CLIC/GCL and current rules.
System: 248 KB; architecture, GSL/process/AAP, engines, knowledge, domains, theory, profiles, lifecycle.
Technical: 805 KB; ontology, grammar, Process Algebra, Knowledge/Proof/Capabilities/Domains, reasoning, numerous technical profiles, T-EH engineering units.
Theories: 164 KB; theory registry + SRT/VSM/RPM/PPM/TFT/FET/SCT + research/reference architectures.
Annexure: 660 KB; dictionary, registries, rights, catalogue, invariants/proofs/tests, CPI/CDDT/OCF/CMUR/CLIC/GCL, current cross-layer rules.

OBSERVED DOCUMENTATION ISSUES
A. Ownership blur
- Same hard-gate, authority-non-accretion, UNKNOWN/non-PASS, rights/privacy/safety principles recur in multiple files.
- Need one normative owner + concise references.

B. Chronological residue
- Current clean source still contains headings such as OWNER-BOUND CANDIDATE / ENGINEERING EXTENSIONS, COMPARATIVE / COGNITIVE / DESIGN-CLOSURE EXTENSIONS, CAUSAL / HUMAN-EFFECT / INSTITUTIONAL HARDENING.
- These group by upgrade wave rather than conceptual ownership.

C. Mixed abstraction levels
- User file sometimes carries technical/algebra details.
- Technical file sometimes carries explanatory prose better suited to User/System.
- Annexure contains normative tables mixed with prose explanations.
- Theories mixes theory definitions, reference architectures and research candidates without uniform template.

D. Repeated boilerplate
Technical exact/repeated patterns include:
- machine-binding unresolved status repeated about 20 times;
- identical FunctionContract boilerplate repeated across many engineering units;
- repeated multi-status non-PASS clauses;
- repeated AnnexRefs.
These should be factored into shared normative conventions + per-unit deltas without losing information.

E. Navigation
- Stable anchors exist, but hierarchy is inconsistent.
- Some headings use numbers, some brackets, some prose.
- Need predictable section templates and canonical cross-reference format.

F. Theory consistency
Current core theory versions in source:
- SRT: no explicit numeric version
- VSM: v2.0
- RPM: v2.0
- PPM: v2.0
- TFT: v1.1
- FET: no explicit numeric version in some places
- SCT: no explicit numeric version in some places
Desired documentation rule:
- Give every core theory an explicit release-visible version/status.
- Do not fake-bump versions due only to Garden integration changes.
- If owned semantics changed, bump version; otherwise preserve semantic version and record binding/composition change separately.

G. GAIA naming gap
Current clean source uses GAIA Titanium / GAIA Diamond but does not contain the full expansion.
Restore:
GAIA = Garden Artificial Intelligence Architecture
Definition should occur once in canonical naming/theory/reference-architecture metadata.

PROPOSED DOCUMENT OWNERSHIP
1. USER / HUMAN DESIGN
   Purpose, principles, rights, sovereignty, conceptual architecture, human-facing explanation, boundaries.
2. SYSTEM / FLOW DESIGN
   Components, control loops, flows, state transitions, interaction of owners, runtime/system behavior.
3. TECHNICAL SPECIFICATION
   Types, schemas, algebras, FunctionContracts, grammar, algorithms, implementation/conformance requirements.
4. THEORIES & REFERENCE ARCHITECTURES
   Theory definitions, equations, assumptions, applicability, falsifiers, validation, reference architectures, research status.
5. ANNEXURE
   Canonical registries, identifiers, rights, invariants, proof obligations, tests, glossary/dictionary, release/current-reading metadata, cross-layer global rules.

PROPOSED STANDARD SECTION TEMPLATES
Normative component:
Purpose
Owner
Status
Inputs / Preconditions
Outputs / Result algebra
Rules
Failure / UNKNOWN behavior
Dependencies / Interfaces
Invariants
Tests / proof obligations
Notes/examples only when they add information

Theory:
Name / Version / Status / Type
Purpose
Formal model
State/variables/operators
Assumptions
Applicability
Falsifiers
Dependencies/composition
Validation evidence/status
Known limits
Garden interfaces

Profile/reference architecture:
Purpose
Status
Owner
Scope
Parameters
Flow
Safety/authority constraints
Operational defaults (qualified vs illustrative)
Failure modes
Tests
Dependencies

REVIEW TASK
Independently challenge this documentation plan.
Return JSON only:
